 density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{5}{6},$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x}{2}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186430391 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{17}{24},$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}, & 0<x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}, & 1\\le x, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186430392 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186430547 "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,3)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0.4, & \\,x=2 \\\\ 0.6, & \\,x=4 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=3]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,3)$ is shown above."] [17592186430549 "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0.3, & \\,x=3 \\\\ 0.7, & \\,x=5 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=2]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)$ is shown above."] [17592186432954 "$$\nF(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5, & x\\in [-6,0] \\\\ -2, & x\\in (0,6)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. The Fourier series of the $12$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{3}{2}-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{14}{\\pi (2n-1)}sin\\,\\left(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi x}{6}\\right).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nAt $x=-3,$ we have\n\n$$\nsin\\,\\left(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi (-3)}{6}\\right)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is \n{{field-2}}\nat $x=-3,$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(-3)={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1}={{field-4}}.\n$$"] [17592186432955 "$$\nF(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2, & x\\in [-\\pi ,0] \\\\ {x}^{2}+3x, & x\\in (0,\\pi )\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. Find the value to which the Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is converging when $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nThe Fourier series converges to {{field-1}} when $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$"] [17592186432956 "$$\nF(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}, & x\\in [-3,0] \\\\ {x}^{2}-1, & x\\in (0,3)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. Find the value to which the Fourier series of the $6$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is converging when $x=-1.$\n\nThe Fourier series converges to {{field-1}} when $x=-1.$"] [17592186432958 "$$\nF(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x, & x\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0] \\\\ {e}^{x}, & x\\in (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. Find the value to which the Fourier series of the $\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is converging when $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\nThe Fourier series converges to {{field-1}} when $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$"] [17592186434097 "Given that the random variable $X∼{χ}^{2}(8),$ calculate $P(X<6).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places.\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{6}{x}^{3}{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x≈33.86574\n$$\n\n*The probability density function ${χ}^{2}(k)$ is given by*\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{2}^{k/2}Γ\\left(\\frac{k}{2}\\right)}{x}^{k/2-1}{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186434098 "Given that $X∼{χ}^{2}(8),$ what is $P(X<6)$ expressed as an integral?\n\n*Hint: The probability density function ${χ}^{2}(k)$ is given by*\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{2}^{k/2}Γ\\left(\\frac{k}{2}\\right)}{x}^{k/2-1}{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186434425 "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x, & 0<x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\,x, & 1\\le x<2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$"] [17592186434814 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]≈1.238\\,10,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{2{x}^{2}}{7}, & 1\\le x<2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186434815 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{8},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186434816 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=0.65,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5}, & 0<x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}, & 1\\le x, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186436042 "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curve ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1.$ If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y), & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,{∬}_{D}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [17592186436043 "![](images/bb/bbc1bc7b3bb910ffbd13571283bbfa305404d13eb2cb3b5ab423a1c02e46ab86.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}) & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply."] [17592186436280 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Give your answer rounded to two decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-1, & 2<x<3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{12}, & 3\\le x<4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186436282 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[4X+2].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}, & 0<x\\le 1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186436283 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[12X-8].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}, & 0<x\\le 1, \\\\ \\frac{8}{9}, & 1\\le x<2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186437252 "Find $\\text{E}[\\sqrt{X}],$ given that the continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186441112 "Suppose we have a population of size $N=75,$ where $80\\%$ of the population has a particular characteristic. Let the random variable ${X}_{i}$ be equal to\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the population has the characteristic} \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nfor $i=1,…,75.$ Find $P({X}_{2}=0|{X}_{1}=0).$"] [17592186441117 "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n=400$ from a population where $32\\%$ of the population has a particular characteristic. Let the random variable ${X}_{i}$ be equal to\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the sample has the characteristic} \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $i=1,…,400.$ If the statistic $X$ is defined as\n\n$$\nX={\\sum }_{i=1}^{400}{X}_{i}\n$$\n\nfind approximate values of $\\text{E}[X]$ and $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.*"] [17592186441118 "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n=130$ from a population where $35\\%$ of the population has a particular characteristic. Let the random variable ${X}_{i}$ be equal to\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the sample has the characteristic} \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $i=1,…,130.$ Find an approximate sampling distribution of the statistic $$\n\\displaystyle X={\\sum }_{i=1}^{130}{X}_{i}.\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.*"] [17592186441119 "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n=180$ from a population where $48\\%$ of the population has a particular characteristic. Let the random variable ${X}_{i}$ be equal to\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the sample has the characteristic} \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $i=1,…,180.$ Find an approximate sampling distribution of the statistic $$\n\\displaystyle X={\\sum }_{i=1}^{180}{X}_{i}.\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.*"] [17592186441120 "A box contains $70$ marbles, of which $30\\%$ are red and the rest are green. Let the random variable ${X}_{i}$ be equal to\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th marble in the box is red} \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nfor $i=1,…,70.$ Find $P({X}_{2}=0|{X}_{1}=0).$"] [17592186441121 "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n=45$ from a population where $20\\%$ of the population has a particular characteristic. Let